{
  "title": "HTTP disk cache: non-atomic writes and errors that hide good responses",
  "description": "ramekin-core/src/http/cache.rs: an entry is absent, success (response.bin + metadata.json), negative (error.txt) or partial. \
Writes aren't atomic (142-146), so a crash can leave response.bin without metadata; get() then misses but is_cached() (67-70) and stats() (186) report a hit. put_error doesn't remove response.bin, and fetch_with_cache checks the error first (http/client.rs:328-335), so a permanent error hides a good cached copy. \
Error permanence is decided by a string prefix match (216-218). \
Want: write to a temp file and rename, one function that classifies an entry, and a typed permanent/transient error marker. make pipeline should produce no data/ diffs; if it does, they're cache entries that were misclassified and worth calling out. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
